<title>MEXICO: Honda looking into making new car in Mexico.</title>
<headline>Honda looking into making new car in Mexico.</headline>
<dateline>GUADALAJARA, Mexico 1996-10-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Honda de Mexico is looking into manufacturing a new family car in Mexico and may make an announcement at the beginning of 1997, the company president said Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;We have the plan, we don't know when it will be,&quot; Hideo Kimura, president of Honda's Mexican subsidiary, told Reuters.</p>
<p>Honda has been making the Accord model since December 1995 at a plant in El Salto, near Mexico's second city of Guadalajara.</p>
<p>Honda de Mexico is a unit of Honda Motor Co Ltd</p>
<p>--Monica Ballesca, Guadalajara bureau +523 817-0397</p>
